02. S3 Bucket vs EBS

| S3                                | EBS                            |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Object storage                    | Block storage                  |
| Regional service                  | AZ-scoped volume               |
| Access through APIs               | Attached to EC2                |
| Great for files/artifacts/backups | Great for OS/application disks |
| Highly durable object storage     | Persistent EC2 block storage   |


Example

EC2 operating system:

EBS
 |
 +-- /var
 +-- /home
 +-- application

Application uploaded images:

S3
 |
 +-- images/



03. S3 vs EFS

| S3                                       | EFS                      |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |
| Object storage                           | File storage             |
| API-based access                         | NFS filesystem           |
| Not mounted like normal Linux filesystem | Can be mounted           |
| Great for artifacts/backups              | Shared filesystem        |
| Massive object storage                   | Shared application files |


